.TH DANBY-MIGRATION 1
.SH NAME
danby-migration \- effects of migration on an SIR epidemic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/migration
.SH MODEL
S' = -beta SI+m(Sm-S);
I' = beta SI-gamma I+m(Im-I);
R' = gamma I-mR.
.PP
Migration replaces residents at rate m with a migrant population having
infectious fraction Im and susceptible fraction Sm=1-Im.  The replacement
form keeps S+I+R constant while allowing continuing importation of infection.
It supersedes the former unrelated two-region logistic demonstration.
.SH DISPLAY
The three histories reveal whether imported cases decay, maintain an endemic
level, or seed a large epidemic.  Current compartments can be changed directly.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag a compartment bar.  Tracks set contact, recovery, migration rate, and
migrant infection fraction.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The regression suite verifies conservation of total population under migration.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/migration.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/migration.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-epidemic (1),
.IR populationmodel (2)
